      "artist": "InSapphoWeTrust from Los Angeles, California, USA",
      "description": "A nice late afternoon beach scene on Ocean Beach, on San Francisco's west end facing the Pacific Ocean.\nThis area remains foggy all day and all night on most summer days, but around Labor Day weekend, when this shot was taken, sunshine and warm temperatures finally arrive. It is also enjoyable, as the only urban beach in the entire San Francisco Bay Area; due to the persistent chill and fog on the ocean side, almost all urban developments in the Bay Area circle the Bay instead.\nAnd to drive that point, these drummers are keeping things upbeat and interesting for beach visitors.\n\nIn the background can be seen a Dutch windmill that is one of the architectural elements of the western end of Golden Gate Park.",
